incibility. They start believing they don't need to compromise with other countries or listen to their own citizens, because they think the oil money will always bail them out. You and your friends are looking at a century of leaders ignoring their people, misjudging their enemies, and making the same mistakes over and over again. At the end of the day, calling that "foolish" isn't missing the nuance—it's just an accurate description of the results.
