print for the peace, art, and coexistence we see in other eras and cultures. This is why taking a course on world religions is so fascinating. It moves you past the question of "Is this religion purely good or purely evil?" and asks the much more interesting question: "How does this ancient system of ideas have the power to inspire both the best and the worst of human behavior, century after century?"
